BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit by TooPink
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T235959
UID:69f4ed88b6c4ac1fedd01243@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of May\, works by artist TooPink are on d
 isplay at Northern District Library branch in an exhibit.\nTooPink is a yo
 ung emerging artist studying at the Ontario College of Art and Design Univ
 ersity. She focuses on interdisciplinarity and passionately studies a wide
  array of art forms and mediums. In addition to analogue photography\, she
  experiments with sculpture\, installation\, drawing\, painting\, film\, a
 nd performance art.\n"TooPink has a deep love for analogue photography and
  historical photographic printing processes. She develops her own lm and a
 lways prints her photos in the darkroom herself\, as she appreciates how m
 uch of the art of photography is done in the processing of the photo. She 
 also experiments with historical photography\, using processes from the 18
 00s such as cyanotype printing and salt printing. Her subject matter range
 s from street photography to nature and wildlife photography."\nThis exhib
 it is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library p
 rovides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across 
 the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of 
 the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during\nNorthe
 rn District\nLibrary open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Northern District\, 2nd floor exhibit area
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f4ed88b6c4ac1fedd01243
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
