BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Money Management and Access to Government Benefits
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T120000
UID:69e1271c129f12743838f4d1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to take control of your finances and make your money
  work for you. This practical workshop facilitated by a financial empowerm
 ent staff member from North York Community House will help you understand 
 your income and expenses\, create a realistic budget\, start saving\, and 
 learn how to access government benefits you may be eligible for\, helping 
 you build a stronger and more secure financial foundation.\nDrop-in welcom
 e!\nNo registration required.
LOCATION:Thorncliffe
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e1271c129f12743838f4d1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Matcha Workshop and Mini Japanese Tea Ceremony
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T193000
UID:69b847902b552e8e21b32eef@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discover more about powdered green tea\, Matcha.  We will exp
 lain all about Matcha:  how/when it is harvested\, and how to make Matcha
  in a traditional way.  Participants will learn how to make traditional M
 atcha\, compare colour/aroma/taste of different grades of Matcha\, and lea
 rn the best types of Matcha to buy.  Participants can also try Japanese t
 raditional sweet Wasanbon (pure sugar treat) which is normally served with
  Matcha.\nOnline registration is required beginning May 25th.\nThis is a p
 rogram for adults.
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b847902b552e8e21b32eef
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
