BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SP Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T150000
UID:698bc9cbcbf6405d356706a7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discuss diverse and inclusive titles from a variety of genres 
 on the fourth Thursday of every month!\nThis month we will be discussing\n
 The Survivalists\nby Kashana Cauley.\nAretha’s single-minded pursuit of 
 a legal partnership is upended when she moves in with her new boyfriend an
 d his roommates—a chaotic group of bunker-building survivalists traumati
 zed by Hurricane Sandy. Instead of climbing the corporate ladder\, she fin
 ds herself sliding into a surreal existence of illegal arms dealing and pr
 otein rations as she trains for a disaster that feels just around the corn
 er.\nPick up a physical copy at the branch before the meeting\, or find co
 pies through our website in various formats. Registration is required and 
 begins May 28\, 2026.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inform
 ation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Pu
 blic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information w
 ill only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluat
 ion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be direc
 ted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge
  Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Canoe Table\, center of branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698bc9cbcbf6405d356706a7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SP Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T150000
UID:698bcaa1cbf6405d356706f4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discuss diverse and inclusive titles from a variety of genres 
 on the fourth Thursday of every month!\nThis month we will be discussing y
 our current or recent reads.\nJoin us for a\nBYOB (Bring Your Own Book) me
 eting\n\, where we swap stories about what we're reading. Simply show up w
 ith a book you've read recently to share a quick review and connect with o
 ther readers. It’s the perfect way to discover your next favorite book w
 ithout the pressure of a deadline.\nRegistration is required and begins Ju
 n. 25\, 2026.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on
  this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Lib
 raries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only
  be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Que
 stions about how the library handles your information can be directed to A
 nswerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\
 , Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Canoe Table\, center of branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698bcaa1cbf6405d356706f4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monday Movies - F1
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T153000
UID:69e653b1b6c4ac1fedcd8d91@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This month's movie:\nF1\nThis movie is rated PG-13\nSonny Haye
 s was Formula 1's most promising phenom of the 1990s until an accident on 
 the track. Thirty years later\, his former teammate Ruben Cervantes convin
 ces him to come back and drive alongside hotshot rookie Joshua Pearce for 
 one last shot at being the best in the world. Sonny's past catches up with
  him and he finds that the road to redemption is not something you can tra
 vel alone.
LOCATION:Cliffcrest
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e653b1b6c4ac1fedcd8d91
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
