BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Reading: Nadja Lubiw-Hazard
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T200000
UID:69950aaf8d5e2d09335fd21f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​Author and veterinarian Nadja Lubiw-Hazard will read from h
 er novel\,\nThe Nap-Away Motel\nand discuss her creative process.\nNadja i
 dentifies as a writer with a disability (bipolar disorder) and as an LGBTQ
  writer. Her novel is based in Toronto\, and grapples with the challenges 
 of mental health\, addiction and grief.\nDrop-in
LOCATION:Runnymede\, Program room\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69950aaf8d5e2d09335fd21f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
